ork soon after in november of  2008 artem launched kick-ass torrents  initially it looks like arthum tried his  best to avoid issues with the  authorities cat proudly claimed that  they complied with the dmca and that  they would remove copyright infringing  torrents as soon as they were notified  but in reality this wasn't exactly the  case given the context of the site it  didn't take long for users to start  uploading copyrighted content and for  copyright holders to start contacting  cat but they were hit with the same  response every single time  greetings your request has been reviewed  but cannot be processed due to one or  more of the following reasons  most of these reasons were complete and  utter bs reason 4 for example was that  there were more than 30 torrents  mentioned in the claim email if cat was  legitimately trying to comply addressing  such a claim would be a top priority but  cat was intentionally avoiding claims  with a large list of torns probably  because they wanted to draw out the  takedown process and to minimize how  many torrents they lost with each  takedown cat was able to get away with  such outright incompliance for many  years as prosecutors had much bigger  fish to fry but as soon as they took  down mega upload and the pirate bay  prosecutors turned their focus to kick  ass torrents  initially prosecutors started off pretty  light against kick-ass they didn't know  who was behind the site and honestly i  don't think they cared they just wanted  to take down the website and stop the  spread of copyrighted material so in  february of 2013 they started working  with internet service providers to block  access to can't the high court in london  ordered isps to block people from  accessing kick ass torrents and to other  torrent sites the isps did comply and  block access but every time they blocked  access to one domain of kick-ass  kick-ass just moved to another domain  they moved from ka.tt to kitkat.to to  ticketcast.eso ticketcasttorrs.im to  cat.cr and so on and so forth clearly  prosecutors couldn't take down the  website through isps but they were able  to force cad to constantly switch  domains this meant that most people  didn't know what the latest domain was  off the top of their heads they had to  google kick-ass torrents to find the  latest link considering this the motion  picture association of america or the  mpaa decided to work with google to take  down kant they asked google to remove  the correct kick-ass link from google  search results they also worked with  steam to prevent the correct link from  being shared on steam chat this strategy  was actually decently effective as this  resulted in many pirates stumbling upon  malicious copycat sites that were filled  with malware and viruses and this was  the perfect excuse for chrome and  firefox to completely block access to  cad even if you had the correct link if  you tried to access cat through these  browsers in late 2015 you got a message  suggesting that they blocked access to  the site because they don't want you to  download a virus it was definitely not  because they were being pressured by  copyright holders they just wanted to  look out for your best interests jokes  aside though we all know why they  blocked axes  in 2016 chrome and firefox changed their  excuse to fishing concerns but soon  enough neither of them wanted to play  these raids anymore so they opened up  axes and stepped out of the way  by this point it was clear that cat  wasn't just a bug that prosecutors could  squash and move on cat had evolved into  being the world's largest fire sharing  site so prosecutors decided that it was  time to go for the host  by this point the fbi had spent years  trying to unsuccessfully take down cat  so they decided to escalate things to  their real top dogs the irs whether it  be al capone or the wolf of wall street  it's clear that the one entity that you  never want to piss off is the irs many  have pissed off the fbi and gotten away  with it for years but almost no one has  escaped the irs and this was no  different for artem the irs didn't care  that artem was causing billions of  dollars worth of lost revenue for  copyright holders but they did care that  artem was causing losses for the irs  you see artem made money off displaying  ads on can't and many of these  advertisers were american yet artem  wasn't paying sales tax or income tax on  this revenue which was a fatal mistake  in march of 2016 the irs got an  undercover agent to inquire about an ad  on cat the irs agent was able to get in  contact with a cat employee named mr  white  mr white informed the agent that cat  charges 300 per ad per day and gave the  agent payment details to a latvian bank  the agent went ahead and bought a  five-day ad in order to gain the trust  of cat and potentially get more details  clearly the irs had motives behind  paying cat but technically this does  also mean that the irs supported cat  with 1500  anyway shortly after the irs agent  contacted mr white again to buy a more  expensive ad this time he was looking at  a banner ad that cost 1 000 to 3200 per  day  it's not clear if the irs actually made  the purchase but they were able to  uncover a new bank account based in  estonia  using these details in conjunction with  the mutual legal assistance treaty  investigators were able to obtain all  the banking records of these two  accounts  this helped the irs figure out that  artem was making bank off of cat at the  peak cat was pulling in nearly 17  million dollars in annual revenue the  irs wanted their cut and fortunately for  them the bank accounts led to more clues  investigators were able to uncover that  the operation was being hosted out of  chicago and that the servers were  located in canada but the most important  piece of evidence they found was  arthem's ip address they didn't know who  the ipaddress belonged to but the walls  were quickly closing in on artem  artem had no idea that prosecutors were  so close to uncovering his identity so  he continued on with his daily life and  this included purchasing media from the  itunes store ironically the owner of the  largest piracy website in the world was  paying for his own media i guess that he  felt that if he had the money you should  pay for it i'm not sure but this  ironically ended up being the root of  his demise you see investigators were  working with a bunch of companies to  track down the ip address one of which  was apple and when artem made a purchase  on the itunes store using his apple id  and his ip address prosecutors were  quickly able to identify him facebook  was also able to provide evidence that  it was in fact artem and the same ip  address that was operating cat's  official facebook account and on july  20th 2016 the department of justice  proudly announced that they were able to  uncover the identity of artem and that  poland police had arrested him they were  also able to shut down cat's proxy  servers and officially take down the  website prosecutors went ahead and  stacked down every copyright  infringement and money laundering charge  they could think of and these were  pretty severe given that cat had  distributed one billion dollars worth of  media according to rtm's lawyer ira  ratkin they were looking to charge up to  20 years for the money laundering and up  to five years for each count of  copyright infringement rothken did  clarify that he highly doubted that all  these charges would actually go through  but worst case scenario arthur could  have been looking at decades in jail to  make things worse arthur was suffering  from extreme back pain and had to be  taken to the hospital artem describes  that during his trip to the hospital he  was escorted by four policemen with  machine guns and one of the guards told  him that they heard that he committed  three murders hearing this arthur knew  that this was going to be more of a  criminal lawsuit than a civil lawsuit  and he had no intention of sticking  around for the verdict  as you might have already guessed as  soon as bail was posted arthur paid the  amount and fled the country the bail  amount was surprisingly only 108  thousand dollars for someone who was  making tens of millions per year  forfeiting even 10 million would have  been an easy price to pay for freedom  but luckily for autumn he only had to  pay a little over a hundred thousand  it's not clear how exactly arthur left  poland given that his passport was  confiscated but given his wealth i'm  sure he was easily able to find a first  class smuggler  anyway on august 26 2020 the polish  ministry of justice confirmed that  arthem had fled the country and the  extradition proceedings would no longer  be continuing in poland his legal team  would drew from the case after they lost  contact with artem and the art and  prosecution has since been put on hold  in other words as long as arthur was  never caught the case will never reach a  verdict and artham can more or less live  a free life in some non-extraditing  country as for kick-ass torrents today  there are many sites trying to emulate  the original but the consensus seems to  be that none of them are as good as the  original also one of the main reasons  that kick-ass became so popular was  because the pirate bay was taken down so  naturally everyone flocked to the second  best option  but with the part babe basically  becoming immortal there seems to be  little need for anything else still many  missed the glory days of cat and the  community behind it while cat was not  able to become immortal like the pirate  bay there's no doubt that cat will  permanently be remembered as a legend in  the piracy community do you guys think  it's moral to pirate comment that down  below also drop a like if kick-ass is  nostalgic for you and of course consider  checking out our international channels  to watch our videos in other languages  and consider subscribing to see more  questions logically answered but until  then i'm hari and i'll see you guys on  the next one  you

